    "function": "Bifunctional enzyme that catalyzes the oxidation and isomerization of cholesterol to cholestenone (cholest-4-en-3-one), an initial step in the cholesterol degradation process. Contributes to virulence. ChoD does not appear to play an essential role in cholesterol degradation in M.tuberculosis, and is probably important for pathogenesis not as a cholesterol-degrading enzyme, but rather as a virulence factor. Required for interference with the host Toll-like receptor 2 (TLR2)-mediated signaling pathway and subsequent intracellular growth and survival of the pathogen in human macrophages. Acts as",
